-- title:
--   Round-six top-level assembly: the κ bound from the round-six interfaces
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa\in\mathbb R$. Assume the six round-six interfaces hold for every admissible parameter record: `SetupNeed6` (the §9.2 setup and sources), `CrtNeed6` ($\Phi$ with the E′ CRT reversal), `FineNeed6` (fine-bit exposure), `LineNeed6` (the line maps), `P14Need6` (the uniform Proposition 14) and `P18IL6` (Proposition 18 from the uniform Proposition 14). Then for every parameter record $P$ with $P.\mathrm{Ok}$ and $\kappa<P.\mathrm{gap}$, if the bit-network histogram satisfies $\mathrm{histMoment}(\mathrm{bitR6},529,P.\tau)<148225616$, the complex-network histogram satisfies $\mathrm{histMoment}(\mathrm{cxR6},576,P.\sigma)<207387136$ and $2+576\log(\mathrm{histRankSum}(\mathrm{cxR6}))\le P.C_1$, the bit network statement `Bit.BitNetR6MomStmt` holds and a complex network interface `Cx.Prop8IfaceH 207387136 T 576 cxR6` exists, then `IntMul.KappaBound κ` holds.
--
